{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919335-minor-templates-and-lunacy","id":919335,"title":"Minor Templates and Lunacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-22T15:01:02-07:00","id":919335,"title":"Minor Templates and Lunacy","content":"I didn't see anything about this in the book and wondered if I might get a clarification or be pointed to the relevant paragraph.<br /> <br /> Currently, the way we're running things in our game is that holders of Minor Templates (aside from Wolf-Blooded) or the Sleepwalker merit are subject to Lunacy but do not explain away what they saw, remembering events unless they suffer a dramatic failure (in which case they don't remember <i>anything</i> after they go nuts) and indeed may potentially become Wolf-Blooded through a dramatic failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:05:27-07:00","id":919336,"title":"","content":"In the first edition, even Wolf Blooded could experience Lunacy, they simply received a positive modifier toward their effective willpower, so I don't see why a Sleepwalker or a Ghoul <i>wouldn't</i> have to deal with it. They still use Integrity, so they still experience the breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:18:39-07:00","id":919390,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't know if you can really consider &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; a template. I think it wouldn't be too unreasonable for Sleepwalkers to be fully susceptible to Lunacy (and probably more likely to encounter it!), but Ghouls would at least be immune to becoming Wolf-Blooded on a Dramatic Failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:41:11-07:00","id":919407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919335-minor-templates-and-lunacy?p=919390#post919390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't know if you can really consider &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; a template. I think it wouldn't be too unreasonable for Sleepwalkers to be fully susceptible to Lunacy (and probably more likely to encounter it!), but Ghouls would at least be immune to becoming Wolf-Blooded on a Dramatic Failure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why is that? it's not as though they lose their Tell if they &lt;s&gt;BECOME VAMPIRE&lt;/s&gt; become a vampire. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes within the course of a chronicle, a Wolf-Blooded character may change her core nature. She may experience the First Change, be ghouled or Embraced by a vampire, be drawn into the Hedge, or even Awaken as a Mage, should the story benefit from those changes. In any of these cases, the Storyteller may require the character lose any Wolf-Blooded Merit she has to reflect her disconnect from Father Wolf and Luna. In this case, consult the Sanctity of Merits rules on p. 105. Unless she goes through the First Change, a Wolf-Blooded character retains her Tell if she becomes another kind of supernatural creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm not sure why being a ghoul would protect them when turning into a vampire or a ghoul does not remove a wolf-blooded's Tell. Ghouls still have Integrity, so they still suffer Lunacy, and any of the resulting conditions that can be afflicted on them.<br /> <br /> At least that's my interpretation of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T00:51:24-07:00","id":919576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919335-minor-templates-and-lunacy?p=919407#post919407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that? it's not as though they lose their Tell if they &lt;s&gt;BECOME VAMPIRE&lt;/s&gt; become a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> In first edition, whether minor templates were susceptible to becoming another minor template was up to ST discretion, the thought being that a character that keeps going through &quot;radiation accidents&quot; to play a game of musical chairs with minor templates might be too silly.<br /> <br /> I'm with you, though, I'd have a ghoul just as likely to become a wolf-blooded as anyone else, but some discretion is necessary.<br /> <br /> Ghosts have integrity, after all, I'm not sure how werewolves would handle someone becoming wolf-blooded post mortem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:55:50-07:00","id":919595,"title":"","content":"I think it's particularly <b>Tell</b>ing that you keep your Tell if you turn into anything other than a Werewolf (per page 300, Changes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T03:36:55-07:00","id":919626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919335-minor-templates-and-lunacy?p=919576#post919576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first edition, whether minor templates were susceptible to becoming another minor template was up to ST discretion, the thought being that a character that keeps going through &quot;radiation accidents&quot; to play a game of musical chairs with minor templates might be too silly.<br /> <br /> I'm with you, though, I'd have a ghoul just as likely to become a wolf-blooded as anyone else, but some discretion is necessary.<br /> <br /> Ghosts have integrity, after all, I'm not sure how werewolves would handle someone becoming wolf-blooded post mortem</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts don't suffer Integrity breaking points unless they're given awareness through Death Magic or the like, and higher ranking ghosts are almost certainly not going to experience a dramatic failure on that.<br /> <br /> I take that to mean they can't be afflicted by Lunacy, at least, since that's how Lunacy operates. Plenty of ghosts are probably trapped in the midst of that breaking point - which is a little horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:42:20-07:00","id":919945,"title":"","content":"Are Mages subject to Lunacy? My ST assumed they weren't for some reason, probably to give me challenge against a cabal of them that my Lone Wolf ended up personally wiping out. We were using 1E rules for it, though, and I don't know much about Mages. I assume that their exposure to altering reality through magic gives them a bit more Willpower to handle Lunacy checks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:45:15-07:00","id":919949,"title":"","content":"No, they don't have Integrity.<br /> <br /> Banishers would, they do still have Integrity and apparently suffer Breaking Points for their own magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:01:04-07:00","id":919964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wayfinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919335-minor-templates-and-lunacy?p=919945#post919945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Mages subject to Lunacy? My ST assumed they weren't for some reason, probably to give me challenge against a cabal of them that my Lone Wolf ended up personally wiping out. We were using 1E rules for it, though, and I don't know much about Mages. I assume that their exposure to altering reality through magic gives them a bit more Willpower to handle Lunacy checks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Members of major templates should be implicitly immune unless they have Integrity for some unfortunate reason, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}